WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:05.672
Journey one: discover businesses. A visitor explores the welcome page,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:09.569
browses home, and opens a category with its filters.

00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:14.441
This run takes the journey from ninety-three percent to complete.

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:19.153
The welcome page is the public landing page for visitors.

00:00:19.153 --> 00:00:23.955
It says what Jubilee is, Toronto's Christian marketplace, and shows the

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:28.689
live count: forty-seven verified businesses in the recorded directory.

00:00:29.391 --> 00:00:33.990
Below are the eleven categories as links, the three steps of how Jubilee

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.311
works, and up to four businesses featured this week.

00:00:38.014 --> 00:00:40.816
Browse businesses opens the browse home.

00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:45.859
A visitor sees the same directory as a member, with a New here panel and

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:48.310
Join free in place of the greeting.

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:53.938
Further down, all forty-seven businesses are grouped by category, each

00:00:53.938 --> 00:00:58.794
group with its count. A group of more than four lists four, and a See

00:00:58.794 --> 00:00:59.427
all link.

00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:03.825
A category with no live businesses has no group.

00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:09.280
Here, no Learning business is live, so Business and tech is followed by

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.505
Media. A new Playwright spec now proves this criterion.

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:17.484
A category chip opens the category page.

00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:22.642
Home and property: ten verified businesses, three of which take

00:01:22.642 --> 00:01:23.952
emergency calls.

00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:29.350
Pressing the Emergency calls chip narrows the list to those three.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:34.045
The filter is kept in the address, so a copied link shows the same

00:01:34.045 --> 00:01:34.543
result.

00:01:35.246 --> 00:01:40.684
Results can be sorted by Recommended, Newest, or Name A to Z.

00:01:40.684 --> 00:01:42.734
Here they are, by name.

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:46.728
These pages are cached for sixty seconds.

00:01:46.728 --> 00:01:51.775
This run settled how the cache is cleared: when the API saves a change

00:01:51.775 --> 00:01:56.750
to a listing, the cached pages are removed, and the next visitor sees

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.796
the change. Decision record three now names this as the designed path.

00:02:02.652 --> 00:02:07.389
Three new API tests prove it through the real endpoints: an owner

00:02:07.389 --> 00:02:12.635
pausing and resuming a listing, a verifier approving one, and a verifier

00:02:12.635 --> 00:02:17.808
setting the featured week. A change made outside the API is seen within

00:02:17.808 --> 00:02:18.828
sixty seconds.

00:02:19.685 --> 00:02:24.473
The requirement, the three designs and their diagrams now describe the

00:02:24.473 --> 00:02:27.414
code as built, and journey one is complete.

00:02:27.414 --> 00:02:32.065
Left for the owner: the visual, responsive and accessibility sweeps,

00:02:32.065 --> 00:02:36.989
which only the owner runs. Page weight and latency budgets belong to the

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.357
performance designs.
